# Repo-root environment — copy to `.env` and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored. This file is the committed template.
#
# ─── Turbo remote cache ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This repository reads its turbo credentials from `.env` and NOWHERE else.
# They are deliberately NOT taken from your shell environment: a single
# `export TURBO_TEAM=...` in a shell profile applies to every repo on the
# machine, which is how a personal project ends up writing to an unrelated
# team's cache. Keeping the values in this file scopes them to this repo.
#
# To fill these in, run once in your terminal:
#
#   turbo login && turbo link
#
# `turbo link` writes `.turbo/config.json` (gitignored) with this repo's team
# ID. That file is what the orchestrator's guard checks TURBO_TEAM against, so
# the two must agree or the remote cache is disabled.
#
# Note: `turbo login` does NOT export anything into your shell — it only writes
# `~/.turbo/config.json`. Copy the values here by hand.
#
# Read `.turbo/config.json` for the team ID, and `~/.turbo/config.json` for the
# token.
TURBO_TOKEN=
TURBO_TEAM=
